[{"text":"CustomIndexNames is an option of FCCanonicalizeDummyIndices. It allows to specify custom names for canonicalized dummy indices of custom index heads.","anchor":"customindexnames"},{"text":"Overview, FCFAConvert, FCCanonicalizeDummyIndices, LorentzIndexNames, CartesianIndexNames.","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"ex = T1[MyIndex2[a], MyIndex1[b]] v1[MyIndex1[b]] v2[MyIndex2[a]] + T1[MyIndex2[c], MyIndex1[f]] v1[MyIndex1[f]] v2[MyIndex2[c]]","anchor":"cb1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\text{v2}(\\text{MyIndex2}(a)) \\;\\text{v1}(\\text{MyIndex1}(b)) \\;\\text{T1}(\\text{MyIndex2}(a),\\text{MyIndex1}(b))+\\text{v2}(\\text{MyIndex2}(c)) \\;\\text{v1}(\\text{MyIndex1}(f)) \\;\\text{T1}(\\text{MyIndex2}(c),\\text{MyIndex1}(f))\\]","anchor":"cb1-2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FCCanonicalizeDummyIndices[ex , Head -> {MyIndex1, MyIndex2}, CustomIndexNames -> {{MyIndex1, {i1}}, {MyIndex2, {i2}}}]","anchor":"cb2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[2 \\;\\text{v1}(\\text{MyIndex1}(\\text{i1})) \\;\\text{v2}(\\text{MyIndex2}(\\text{i2})) \\;\\text{T1}(\\text{MyIndex2}(\\text{i2}),\\text{MyIndex1}(\\text{i1}))\\]","anchor":"cb2-2","section":"Examples"}]